WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:03.084
What if every train in India
stopped for twenty four hours?

00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:07.214
More than twenty million people
travel by train in India every day.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.010
That's nearly the whole population
of Australia, every single day.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.850
If trains stopped,
workers couldn't reach their offices.

00:00:14.091 --> 00:00:16.201
Stations would fill with
stranded travellers.

00:00:16.381 --> 00:00:17.711
Students would miss exams.

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:18.772
Then the freight.

00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:21.732
Trains carry coal, grain,
fertiliser and fuel.

00:00:21.877 --> 00:00:24.887
Power plants depend on coal
wagons arriving on time.

00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:28.718
Within hours, supply chains would
begin to stall across the country.

00:00:28.738 --> 00:00:30.168
The country runs on tracks.

00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:33.614
So what if every train in India
stopped for twenty four hours?

